    "submission": "submission-value-codec.json",
    "summary": "Turn 57 fixed the framing and filed the codec truncation as a formal check.\n\nThe three fixes, each traceable to a validator rule. First, the question's activity context was still A7 while the selected behavior B11-prepare-resolution carries A3 with an attributed A1 cross-activity effect; the validator requires at least one core activity, so the question now declares A1. Second, the supporting behaviors' own sources (durable record, client reply, execution) had to be cited, so they are now in the question's source list alongside the codec and configuration ranges. Third, the binding's symbol had to be a verified declaration: the validator's declaration identity for that range is owner Value, symbol Marshal, lines 230-240, not the dotted form I used.\n\nWhat is now filed. A new obligation C10-command-value-length-survives-the-wire (implementation semantics): the command codec must carry the value length the client's configured command size permits, so a value the client can build must either survive a marshal/unmarshal round trip unchanged or be rejected, never silently shortened. The check round-trips one 70000-byte value through the real codec with the built value as a prerequisite, the codec declaration as its binding, and an assertion that the decoded value matches; the local construction run gives 70013 bytes on the wire, 4464 bytes decoded and 4477 bytes consumed with value_matches false, so the trusted runner is expected to record the truncation as a violation. The claim's scope states the bounded importance (the shipped configuration's 1000-byte commands are inside the field's range), the excluded parts (what a reader does after the stream shifts) and the unknowns (whether the client caps the size it builds).\n\nContext. The codec and configuration ranges are registered as sources, the map is unchanged, and the nine settled claims plus the two paused candidates are untouched. The finding joins the durability family as another place where a value the implementation accepts is not faithfully carried, and it is now reviewable on its own terms rather than only recorded as construction knowledge."
